# Intent: a test hook so the tailnet path can be proven at home (owner 2026-11-14): the device command self.network.prefer_tailnet(minutes) makes the voice and avatar channels skip the home address and use the tailnet hub address for that many minutes (an open link is reopened through the tailnet at once). Off by default, never saved to flash (a restart clears it), refused with tailnet_not_ready while the tailnet is not up. It is an MCP tool, so only the authenticated hub connection can call it.
# Check after a flash: self.network.prefer_tailnet(5) answers {"ok":true,"minutes":5}; the serial log says "Tailnet preferred: reconnecting through the tailnet" then "fallback host for attempt N: <tailnet address> (tailnet preferred)" and the hub sees the unit from a 100.64.0.0/10 address; five minutes later the next reconnect uses the home address again.
